- A solo doctor, individual practitioner, or private cabinet (psychiatrist/psychologist/addictologue working alone).
- A general psychiatric or mental health clinic where addiction treatment is not the primary, formal program.
- A general clinic, polyclinic, or medical center without clear addiction-treatment services.
- Sober living, wellness retreats, or coaching centers without a formal, evidence-based addiction treatment program.
- A smoking-cessation / laser / anti-tobacco service.
- An awareness-only, prevention-only, harm-reduction-only, or advocacy association that does not itself treat patients.
- An unrelated business, hotel, spa, school, pharmacy, or shop.

REVIEW when none of the DROP conditions above confidently apply, but you also cannot confirm every
KEEP condition — e.g. the name/category/address suggests a genuine addiction-treatment facility
(rehab, detox, therapeutic community, narcology, addictology) but you are unsure whether it is
residential vs. outpatient, or unsure of its ownership. REVIEW preserves it for a closer,
evidence-based look rather than guessing KEEP or DROP. Do not use REVIEW for a candidate that
clearly matches a DROP condition, and do not use REVIEW just to avoid committing when the
evidence is actually sufficient for KEEP or DROP.

A false keep is worse than a false review, and a false drop (losing a genuine facility because its
Phase 1 metadata alone was incomplete) is worse than a false review. When genuinely unsure which of
DROP/KEEP applies, prefer REVIEW.

